<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Blackfoot Confederacy</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1877 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The alliance of the Siksika, Kainai and Piikani, horse-mounted bison hunters who dominated the north-western Plains from the Saskatchewan River to the Missouri.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Niitsitapi, Algonquian-speaking peoples of the plains and parklands at the foot of the Rocky Mountains, had long hunted bison on foot. In the early 18th century they acquired horses from the south and guns from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> middlemen trading with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siksika">Siksika</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kainai-nation">Kainai</a> and Piikani emerged as an allied military power.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Each nation was divided into bands led by chiefs chosen for skill in war and generosity, and men's societies policed the summer camps and the communal hunt. Bison provided nearly everything: food, tipis, clothing and tools. The confederacy traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a> posts but kept American trappers out of its lands for decades. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">Smallpox</a> epidemics in 1781, 1837 and 1869 killed many.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Blackfoot had signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lame-bull-treaty">Lame Bull Treaty</a> with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> in 1855; weakened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marias-massacre">Marias Massacre</a> of 1870 and the near extinction of the bison, they signed Treaty 7 with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-canada">Canada</a> in 1877, negotiated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crowfoot">Crowfoot</a>. Today they live on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siksika">Siksika</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kainai-nation">Kainai</a> and Piikani reserves in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberta">Alberta</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blackfeet-reservation">Blackfeet Reservation</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/blackfoot-confederacy.jpg" alt="Blackfoot Confederacy" width="320" height="180"><figcaption>Image: Blackfoot Confederacy. &quot;The tipi ring is captured on the Blackfoot Confederacy Flag, designed by Blood Tribe Grandfat... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Blackfoot_Confederacy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1877 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Crowfoot, Red Crow, Lame Bull</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Blackfoot traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Blackfoot</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a>, <a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Niitsitapi, Siksikaitsitapi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1788&amp;focus=blackfoot-confederacy" aria-label="Blackfoot Confederacy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2554 159 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Blackfoot Confederacy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2874 415h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2874 415h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Canada. <a href="/atlas?year=1788&amp;focus=blackfoot-confederacy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

